==English==

===Etymology===
from [[w:Samuel Plimsoll|Samuel Plimsoll]], Bristol merchant and member of Parliament; promoter of the ''Merchant Shipping Act''.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|head=[[Plimsoll]] [[line]]}}

# {{nautical}} Properly the [[International Load Line]], a mark on the [[hull]] of a [[merchant ship]] to show the [[waterline]] under specified conditions. The line shows the maximum capacity load the ship may carry.

====Related terms====
* [[Plimsoll mark]]
